            <ArticleTitle>[Hybrid revascularization: a combined approach to multivessel coronary artery lesions].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>62-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Analysis of effectiveness and feasibility of hybrid approach to multivessel coronary artery disease and problems of interaction between cardiac surgeons and interventional cardiologists in deciding on the choice of revascularization method is performed in the article. Hybrid approach to multivessel disease defined as sternal sparing, off-pump, minimally invasive, hand sewn left internal mammary - left anterior descending (LAD) arteries by-pass graft with percutaneous coronary revascularization of non-LAD lesions to achieve functionally complete revascularization is described in detail. Data of multicenter studies and clinical recommendations for myocardial revascularization is discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
